* Both kinds of signal in one deck, for the signal-metadata convention
* (book/user-guide/src/signal-metadata.md).
*
*  - V(a)/V(b)/V(d), I(V1)/I(V2)/I(L1): circuit quantities, volts and amps.
*  - DUTY, SCALED: signal-flow values. 0.42 is a duty cycle; nothing in the
*    netlist says what unit it has, and nothing may invent one.
*  - VPROBE, IPROBE: phys2sig, which names the node and the branch it reads,
*    so the netlist does fix their units.
*  - DRIVE: sig2phys, which declares the domain it drives, likewise.
V1 a 0 5
R1 a b 1k
R2 b 0 1k
L1 b 0 1e-3
VPROBE kind=phys2sig node=b
IPROBE kind=phys2sig branch=L1
DUTY kind=const value=0.42
SCALED kind=gain in=DUTY k=2
DRIVE kind=sig2phys domain=voltage in=SCALED
V2 d 0 DRIVE
R3 d 0 1k
MDUTY kind=measure type=avg out=DUTY
MVB kind=measure type=avg out=V(b)
